    "description": "Data Incident & Recovery: Developed a C# microservice deployed on AWS EKS/Docker to recover missing DynamoDB orders, routing batch processing through SQS to Kinesis Data Streams. Mitigated a major production incident by restoring $1.5M+ in critical orders.\nLegacy Code Quality & Testing: Built unit/integration test suites covering 30k+ lines of legacy C# .NET code, raising SonarQube coverage from 57% to 92%. Prepared systems for Chase Atlas migration and freed 15+ story points per sprint.\nAI-Assisted Migration Validation: Leveraged GitHub Copilot to automate SQL export validation against GraphQL schemas for a Frosch VWT data migration to Cassandra. Caught and corrected 1,000+ production record errors, keeping go-live timelines on track.\nHigh-Value Client Integration: Architected cross-LOB integrations using Java, React.js, GraphQL, and Salesforce for bespoke concierge servicing. Retained $500M+ in UHNW assets and unlocked a new revenue stream.\nSecure PCI Data Migration: Built a Python utility to securely extract and migrate high-end client payment data from legacy SQL Server and Azure Key Vault to Chase PCI tokenization endpoints, ensuring seamless Salesforce integration with zero friction.\nFrontend & CRM Engineering: Released a secure credit card detokenization UI component (LitElement, React, TypeScript) in Salesforce CRM, allowing advisors to process orders using 16-digit PANs and boosting CSAT scores.\n Large-Scale Enterprise Migration: Engineered a C# .NET pipeline to migrate 100,000+ production orders from SQL Server to AuroraDB and Cassandra, enabling Chase Atlas onboarding for a pilot group of travel advisors.\nArchitectural Innovation (AI/ML): Designed the C.A.R.E. framework to score customer attrition risk via transactional deltas and sentiment analysis, utilizing AI-generated pain summaries and proactive Streamlined AWS environment provisioning using Terraform, reducing infrastructure setup time to <24 hours and lowering operational overhead.",
